      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find \\(3 \\oplus 1\\), we need to use the operation defined by \\(a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\\). This means we substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\) into the expression \\(3a + 4b\\).\n\nFirst, let's substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\) into the expression \\(3a + 4b\\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\oplus 1 = 3(3) + 4(1)\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the multiplications:\n\n\\[\n3(3) = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n4(1) = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the results of the multiplications together:\n\n\\[\n9 + 4 = 13\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{13}\\).",
