      "text": "To solve for \\(3 \\oplus 1\\) given the operation \\(a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\\), we will substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\) into the given operation.\n\nFirst, we write down the operation:\n\\[\na \\oplus b = 3a + 4b\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = 1\\):\n\\[\n3 \\oplus 1 = 3(3) + 4(1)\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplications:\n\\[\n3(3) = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n4(1) = 4\n\\]\n\nThen, we add the results together:\n\\[\n9 + 4 = 13\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{13}\n\\]",
